w: God, be mer- ci- ful to me, On Thy grace I rest my plea;
w: My trans- gress- ions I con- fess, Grief and guilt my soul op- press;
w: I am ev- il, born in sin; Thou de- sir- est truth with- in.
w: Bro- ken, humbl- ed to the dust By Thy wrath and judg- ment just,
w: Gra- cious God, my heart re- new, Make my spir- it right and true;
w: Sin- ners then shall learn from me And re- turn, O God, to Thee;
E G B B | c c B2 | E G B B | c c B2 |
w: Plen- teous in com- pas- sion Thou, Blot out my trans- gress- ions now;
w: I have sinned a- gainst Thy grace And pro- voked Thee to Thy face;
w: Thou a- lone my Sa- vior art, Teach Thy wis- dom to my heart;
w: Let my con- trite heart re- joice And in glad- ness hear Thy voice;
w: Cast me not a- way from Thee, Let Thy Spir- it dwell in me;
w: Sa- vior, all my guilt re- move, And my tongue shall sing Thy love;
E E F G | A3/2 A/ G2 | E F G F | E D E2 |]
w: Wash me, make me pure with- in, Cleanse, O cleanse me from my sin.
w: I con- fess Thy judg- ment just, Speech- less, I Thy mer- cy trust.
w: Make me pure, Thy grace be- stow, Wash me whit- er than the snow.
w: From my sins O hide Thy face, Blot them out in bound- less grace.
w: Thy salv- at- ion’s joy im- part, Stead- fast make my wil- ling heart.
w: Touch my si- lent lips, O Lord, And my mouth shall praise ac- cord.
